- Test build on non-NetBSD platforms. At least manual compilation from
  source works with NetBSD, FreeBSD, OpenBSD and DragonflyBSD, and
  cross-compilation to MacOS works with zig cc and the resulting amd64
  Mac binary runs on MacOS emulator "darling". The code should be
  POSIX compliant, but what POSIX doesn't specify is linker arguments
  so on some POSIX systems, it might require linking to some other
  libraries than libc and libm.
